%N A400358 Decimal expansion of (3 - sqrt(6))/2.
%C A400358 Largest possible minimal pairwise distance of eleven points inside an equilateral triangle with unit side length.
%C A400358 Equivalently, largest diameter of the circles in the densest packing of eleven equal circles inside an equilateral triangle with side length equal to 1 + sqrt(3)*(this constant). If the circles had unit radius, the corresponding triangle would have side length A399815.
%H A400358 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400358/b400358.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400358 Hans (J. B. M.) Melissen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2307/2324212">Densest Packings of Congruent Circles in an Equilateral Triangle</a>, The American Mathematical Monthly, Vol. 100, Issue 10 (1993), pp. 916-925 (also available on <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324212">JSTOR</a>).
%H A400358 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_packing_in_an_equilateral_triangle">Circle packing in an equilateral triangle</a>.
%H A400358 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_02">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 2</a>.
%F A400358 Equals (3 - A010464)/2.
%F A400358 Equals 2/(A399815 - 2*A002194).
%F A400358 Equals the smallest root of 4*x^2 - 12*x + 3.
%F A400358 Equals 2 - A379800 = A393353^2. - _Hugo Pfoertner_, Oct 03 2026
%e A400358 0.27525512860841095090135796264705430401702625967166...
%t A400358 First[RealDigits[(3 - Sqrt[6])/2, 10, 100]]
%Y A400358 Analogous values for k points: 1 (k = 2, 3), A020760 (k = 4), A020761 (k = 5, 6), A152422 (k = 7), A400357 (k = 8), A010701 (k = 9, 10), A019913 (k = 12), A400359 (k = 13), A020773 (k = 14, 15).
%Y A400358 Cf. A379800, A393353, A399815.
%Y A400358 Cf. A002194, A010464.
%K A400358 nonn,cons,easy,new
%O A400358 0,1
